# Deterministic output is compared byte for byte across operating systems (snapshots, generated code),
# so the working tree uses LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
# The corpus is third-party and vendored byte for byte (tests/corpus/README.md): its hashes are checked against the
# manifest, so git must not convert its line endings.
tests/corpus/sql-server-samples/** -text
# The plots fixture is about how scripts are laid out: byte order marks, UTF-16, CRLF and a lone CR. Git must keep its
# scripts byte for byte (tests/fixtures/plots/README.md).
tests/fixtures/plots/database/** -text
